From c5615d71a2a375e7b00f07e520dd33db770da4a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:08:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Fix CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (backport to
 5.6.40)

Semantic port of upstream php-src commit 712e60f9ed "Avoid state
corruption via bailout" (Arnaud Le Blanc, Ilija Tovilo), branch
PHP-7.4-CVE-2026-109618-109619, GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w / GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp.
The 5.6 engine differs too much for the hunks to apply; each change is
re-done for the 5.6 code:

CVE-2026-109618 (no bailout out of an allocation failure):
- zend_mm_safe_error_ex() added (zend_alloc.c/.h): prints the fatal
  error with file/line to stderr and _exit(1)s. zend_mm_safe_error()
  (memory_limit, "Out of memory") now calls it instead of
  zend_error()+zend_bailout(); the heap->reserve/overflow dance goes.
- safe_address() overflow (6 sites) and _safe_emalloc_string() overflow
  use it; zend_mm_panic() and __zend_malloc/__zend_realloc use _exit.
- zend_strtod.c Balloc(): both fatal errors.
- zend_operators.c: the four "String size overflow" checks in
  add_char_to_string/add_string_to_string/concat_function - in 5.6 the
  ZEND_CONCAT/ZEND_ASSIGN_CONCAT handlers go through these, they are the
  equivalent of the VM concat checks in the 7.4 patch.
  smart_str, ZVAL_STRING and ext/standard are left alone, as upstream.

CVE-2026-109619 (no request state survives into the next request):
- shutdown_executor(): EG(error_handling)/EG(exception) reset after the
  object store is freed; the handler stacks are cleared after destroy
  (zend_ptr_stack_destroy leaves dangling element pointers);
  objects_store.top = 1. Handlers themselves were already NULLed in 5.6.
- zend_llist_destroy(): head/tail = NULL.
- sapi_deactivate(): freed request_info pointers set to NULL.
- php_request_shutdown() and php_request_shutdown_for_hook():
  PG(http_globals)[i] = NULL after the dtor; PG(modules_activated) = 0.
- session: rfc1867 upload-progress callback disabled unconditionally.
- rfc1867: only Content-Disposition/Content-Type headers kept, duplicates
  ignored; size_t in substring_conf(); max_multipart_body_parts (new INI,
  default -1 = max_input_vars + max_file_uploads).
- php_variables.c: request-variable arrays start small
  (array_init_singleton). nTableSize is 2, not 1: in the 5.6 hash
  nTableMask == 0 marks an unallocated bucket array (CHECK_INIT), and a
  table of 1 would have mask 0.

Behaviour change: memory_limit exhaustion no longer runs shutdown
functions or error handlers; the process exits (php-fpm respawns the
child). Session upload progress is gone.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
