From 9dcbe9f92d7aaccc6e6957ddc7f431c32b9c0892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:50:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Fix GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv (CVE-2026-129496):
 DATEG(tzcache) use-after-free in php_log_err

Backport of php-src cb20015e04 ("Fix GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv: DATEG(tzcache)
use-after-free", PHP-8.2).

php_log_err() formatted the error_log timestamp in local time whenever
it was not in ZTS module startup. Local time goes through
php_date_parse_tzfile(), which allocates DATEG(tzcache) with emalloc. A
message logged while ext/date is not active (module startup, request
startup before date's RINIT, after its RSHUTDOWN) left DATEG(tzcache)
pointing into memory the memory manager then freed; the next log line
before RINIT reset it (e.g. a client-triggered "Input variables
exceeded" warning during php_hash_environment) used the freed table.
Use local time only while modules are activated and the executor is
active; otherwise the timestamp is UTC.

Differences from upstream:
- 5.6 php_format_date() returns char* and takes TSRMLS_DC; the whole
  #ifdef ZTS / php_during_module_startup() block is replaced by one call
  with `PG(modules_activated) && EG(active) TSRMLS_CC`, as upstream.
  php_during_module_startup() stays (still used by php_error_cb).
- zend_test parts skipped (no zend_test in 5.6).
- Test: GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv.phpt adapted: {PWD} instead of {TMP}, and a
  startup warning from a failing `extension=` load instead of
  zend_test.warn_on_startup; display_startup_errors=0 so only the
  request-startup warning is shown. Meant to be run with valgrind (-m);
  without it the UAF may not crash.

Behaviour change (same as upstream): lines logged to error_log outside
an active request (startup, request startup, late shutdown) carry a UTC
timestamp instead of date.timezone.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
